  "notes": "Frozen ground truth (v1.4.0). v1.3.0 closes the gaps that BOTH competitor runs exposed: /metrics exposure, /support/logs listing, error-stack disclosure, JWT carrying the password hash, basket BOLA, and customer-created products. Every item hand-verified against the pinned image. v1.4.0 adds the last three items competitors reported: free deluxe membership (paymentMode=none), security-question user enumeration, and negative basket quantity. v1.5.0 expands the DVWA catalogue from 5 to 8 items: stored XSS, arbitrary file upload (PHP executes), and CSRF password change. v1.6.0 closes the last capability gap: DVWA blind SQLi (boolean differential), DOM XSS (source→sink), and unauthenticated user-data API (IDOR/BFLA) — all reported by competitors but previously not probed by us. v1.6.1: DV-11 reworded — the endpoint requires a session (anonymous returns 404), so it is BFLA (any authenticated user reads all users), not unauthenticated access. v1.6.2: DV-11 removed — /vulnerabilities/authbypass/get_user_data.php returned 200 on one build/session state and 404 on a clean rebuild, so it fails the 'deterministically reachable' inclusion criterion. It stays an extra-tp in adjudications instead of a catalogue item.",
